# .public-exclude — files a human has REVIEWED and deliberately kept private.
#
# Unlike .public-deny (a permanent fuse for whole categories), this is where
# `python scripts/classify_public.py` records case-by-case "keep private"
# decisions, so it won't ask about the same file twice and `--check` stays
# green. Deny-by-default already keeps these private; listing them here just
# marks them as consciously-decided rather than merely un-reviewed.
#
# You normally don't edit this by hand — the interactive classifier appends to it.
